  "question": {
    "text": "When equal volume of \\(1 \\mathrm{M} \\mathrm{HCl}\\) and \\(1 \\mathrm{M} \\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{SO}_4\\) are separately neutralised by excess volume of \\(1 \\mathrm{M}\\) \\(\\mathrm{NaOH}\\) solution. \\(x\\) and \\(y \\mathrm{~kJ}\\) of heat is liberated respectively. The value of \\(y / x\\) is _______",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{H}^{+}+\\mathrm{OH}^{-} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O} \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{x} \\\\ & 2 \\mathrm{H}^{+}+2 \\mathrm{OH}^{-} \\rightarrow 2 \\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O} \\Rightarrow 2 \\mathrm{x}=\\mathrm{y} \\\\ & \\mathrm{y} / \\mathrm{x}=2\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
